    pr_ref:  # 6b22
    description: "WHAT\nA Rust call written `Type::method(..)` names its owner. When `Type::method` is not a symbol of the tree, the analyzer falls back to the short name and binds the file's own method of that name, at 0.85:\n  use std::process::Command;\n  pub struct A;  impl A { pub fn new() -> Self { A } }\n  pub fn f() { let s = String::new(); let c = Command::new(\"ls\"); let p = std::path::Path::new(\"x\"); }\nAll three calls are edges f -> A::new (fixture ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/hupis_11242026/probe/scoped_new; run analyze_rust, print the calls edges). `String` is a prelude type, `Command` is imported from std by a `use` in the file, and the third call is written with its full std path.\nWith TWO methods named `new` in the file the INV-hupis fix leaves these calls unresolved (the tie is refused). With one, the short name still binds it: that case is this item.\n\nSEEN ON A REAL REPOSITORY (base arm, dev 81d89b52c, ripgrep): crates/cli/src/decompress.rs lines 137, 182, 501 (`Path::new(..)`, `Command::new(..)`) were edges to DecompressionReader::new; crates/globset/src/glob.rs line 338 (`String::new()`) to GlobBuilder::new; crates/printer/src/standard.rs line 130 (`RefCell::new(..)`) to PreludeWriter::new. Those files declare several `new`, so after the fix they are unresolved. No count was made of the single-`new` files.\n\nEXPECTED: `X::m(..)` binds a method only when its owner is X (or X is `Self`, an alias of the owner, a trait the owner implements, or a type parameter); otherwise it is unresolved. rust.py already has the evidence for a FIELD receiver (_rust_type_is_external: a prelude type, a path rooted outside the tree, a name a `use` brought in from outside) and does not apply it to a scoped call.\nNOT DONE: no count on the corpus; the other analyzers were not checked for the same fallback.\n\nTHE OTHER HALF, same call form: a path call that names its trait is not bound to that trait.\n  <Self as QueryFragment<DB, DB::EmptyFromClauseSyntax>>::walk_ast(self, pass)      (diesel/src/query_builder/from_clause.rs:24)\n  T::py_gc_traverse(self, visit)                                                    (pydantic-core/src/py_gc.rs:39)\nBefore the INV-hupis fix these were edges to whichever impl of the method the file declared last; after it they are unresolved when the file declares the method more than once (the fix binds the trait's declaration for `recv.m()` only, because a path call's own text may name ANOTHER trait: firecracker src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/vhost_user.rs:231, `<Frontend as VhostUserFrontend>::get_protocol_features(self)` inside this file's own trait of the same method name).\nEXPECTED: `<X as T>::m(..)` and `T::m(..)` reach T::m when T is a trait of the tree."  # 6b22
    fields: {}  # 6b22
